  "explanation": "The question asks for the formation date of the National Indian Association. Multiple sources provide conflicting claims:\n\n- D2S8 states the National Indian Association was formed on January 1, 1900.\n- D3S6 and D4S6 state it was formed in 1870 by Mary Carpenter in Bristol.\n- D5S3 states it was initially founded in 1879 in reaction to the opening of Oklahoma Indian Territory.\n- D6S2 and D3S1 mention the formation in Bristol by Mary Carpenter.\n\nEach of these claims refers to the same name 'National Indian Association,' but the contexts differ significantly (e.g., British India vs. U.S. American Indian advocacy). These are distinct referents with overlapping names. Therefore, all four claims are preserved as valid answers."
}
